From 8a916e9a6357cdcd3610490cee35adfc970f3fc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 07:56:38 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Agent: fix MLO backhaul VLAN tagging and AP MLD operational
 status

Fix VLAN tagging and status-detection issues specific to MLO backhaul
connections:

- Resolve the correct per-link BSSID for MLO clients in
  process_client_association() instead of storing the AP MLD MAC in
  client.bssid. The mismatch meant client.bssid never matched the WDS
  notification's bssid, so the WDS interface was never VLAN-tagged.

- Add sta_wlan_hal::get_multi_ap_primary_vlan_id() (and WHM
  implementation) to read the endpoint's MultiAPVlanId without pushing
  an event.

- In BackhaulManager, reassociate on the bSTA interface that reports a
  non-zero MultiAPVlanId (the anchor link) instead of the first
  connected interface, so the resulting Connected event carries the
  correct VLAN ID. Also handle the case where a non-anchor link's
  Connected event itself carries a non-zero VLAN ID: update
  primary_vlan_id, record the interface in the new
  AgentDB::mlo_primary_bsta_iface field, and re-trigger VLAN policy
  application.

- In TrafficSeparationTask::add_backhaul_connection_trunk(), use
  mlo_primary_bsta_iface as the trunk port for MLO backhauls instead of
  the per-link interface, since only the primary interface carries
  real traffic.

- Add slave_thread::is_ap_mld_operationally_up(), which checks all BSS
  entries sharing an AP MLD MAC for an up-and-running interface. Some
  platforms implement a multi-link AP as a single fused interface
  while prplMesh still registers one BSS entry per radio, so only one
  entry's own interface ever comes up. Use this helper alongside the
  existing per-interface check in
  refresh_backhaul_bss_enabled_and_retrigger_wds_ts() and
  update_vaps_info() so MLO fronthaul BSSes are correctly detected as
  enabled.

- In hal_event_handler(), check the return of create_vs_message() for
  both APPLY_VLAN_POLICY_REQUEST sends before calling send_cmdu(), so a
  failed message allocation cannot result in an invalid CMDU being
  transmitted.

- Guard the non-anchor-link VLAN update path with a check that the
  backhaul is currently wireless and that the reporting interface is
  not the already-selected one, so the anchor link's own
  reconnect/roam events (handled by the branch above) cannot retrigger
  this path and overwrite a correct VLAN ID.

Signed-off-by: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
